To determine whether the scoliosis is right or left thoracic, I need to carefully assess the curvature of the spine in the provided chest X-ray. The image has an "L" marker on the top right corner (viewer's right), which typically indicates the patient's left side in standard radiographic convention (PA view). However, sometimes markers indicate the side of the film or are placed differently. Let's verify the orientation and then inspect the spine.

I will use `chest_xray_expert` to ask specifically about the spinal curvature direction relative to the patient's anatomy, and also check the orientation marker interpretation.

